{"name":"Kite Day","hex":"#bad9e5","fetched":"2026-10-18","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kite","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bird of prey of the family Accipitridae.","Any bird of the subfamily Milvinae, with long wings and weak legs, feeding mostly on carrion and spending long periods soaring; specifically, the red kite (Milvus milvus) and the black kite (Milvus migrans)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cause (something) to move upwards rapidly like a toy kite; also  to cause (something, such as costs) to increase rapidly.","To tamper with a document or record by increasing the quantity of something beyond its proper amount so that the difference may be unlawfully retained; in particular, to alter a medical prescription for this purpose by increasing the number of pills or other items."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kite"},{"term":"day","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-5 language code for Land Dayak languages."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is above the horizon and it lights the sky.","A period of time equal or almost equal to a full day-night cycle, being 24 hours long."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/day"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kite","blocks":[{"text":"A kite is a tethered heavier-than-air craft with wing surfaces that react against the air to create lift and drag forces. A kite consists of wings, tethers and anchors. Kites often have a bridle and tail to guide the face of the kite so the wind can lift it. Some kite designs do not need a bridle; box kites can have a single attachment point. A kite may have fixed or moving anchors that can balance the kite. The name is derived from the kite, the hovering bird of prey. There are several kite shapes, including the popular delta kite and diamond kite."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Kitesflying.jpg/330px-Kitesflying.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kite","wikidata":"Q42861"},{"title":"Day","blocks":[{"text":"A day is the time period of a full rotation of the Earth with respect to the Sun. On average, this is 24 hours. As a day passes at a given location it experiences morning, afternoon, evening, and night. This daily cycle drives circadian rhythms in many organisms, which are vital to many life processes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Day","wikidata":"Q573"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Kitesflying.jpg/500px-Kitesflying.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Kitesflying.jpg/500px-Kitesflying.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Various kites being flown","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKitesflying.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Kinderspiele_1828_Drachensteigen.jpg/500px-Kinderspiele_1828_Drachensteigen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Kinderspiele_1828_Drachensteigen.jpg/500px-Kinderspiele_1828_Drachensteigen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Boys flying a kite. Engraving published in Germany in 1828 by Johann Michael Voltz","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKinderspiele_1828_Drachensteigen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7d/Cody_manlifter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7d/Cody_manlifter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"One of Cody's \"manlifter\" kites in 1908","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACody_manlifter.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Kite333.JPG/500px-Kite333.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Kite333.JPG/500px-Kite333.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A quad-line traction kite, commonly used as a power source for kite surfing","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKite333.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Man_flying_kite_on_the_beach.jpg/500px-Man_flying_kite_on_the_beach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Man_flying_kite_on_the_beach.jpg/1280px-Man_flying_kite_on_the_beach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Man_flying_kite_on_the_beach.jpg/500px-Man_flying_kite_on_the_beach.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A man flying a kite on the beach, a good location for flying as winds travelling across the sea contain few up or down draughts which cause kites to fly erratically","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMan_flying_kite_on_the_beach.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Image_taken_from_page_64_of_%27Travels_in_India%2C_including_Sinde_and_the_Punjab%3B_..._translated_from_the_German%2C_by_H._E._Lloyd%27_%2811024411234%29.jpg/500px-Image_taken_from_page_64_of_%27Travels_in_India%2C_including_Sinde_and_the_Punjab%3B_..._translated_from_the_German%2C_by_H._E._Lloyd%27_%2811024411234%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Image_taken_from_page_64_of_%27Travels_in_India%2C_including_Sinde_and_the_Punjab%3B_..._translated_fr